
I haven't tested these demos on systems other than mine, so I am not sure how 
they might look on yours. I have chosen the numbers in these demos as what I thought best fit
my best system. It might look off in yours. 

You may adjust the numbers as you please. I recommend adjusting the dimensions of the declared image 
and the fov (last parameter) of the declared observer as these don't change what the demo is trying 
to show but might make it look better on your screen. If you choose to adjust the image, make sure
it is still centered on (0,0) (that is, it is of the form new ZImage(-x,x,-y,y) for positive
integers x,y). You should also adjust your console font size, as the default one is way too big
for this project. 

For reference, here is a video of me running the TexturedShape demo. My console font 
size is 5 and my screen resolution is 1600 x 1000.

https://files.catbox.moe/jnjyyf.mp4

One last note: these demos don't display the full functionality of my project as I only started developing
them recently. I will start making demos as I add new features. 

Thank you for checking out my project!
